# Security Considerations

DKIM2 will sign the CanModify header field so it cannot be removed
or modified without leaving evidence of this having occurred.

The CanModify merely specifies a request by a message originator.
Receivers are free to determine what to do if this request cannot
be honored, or it is found that an intermediary has not honored it.

